  "equipment_type": "EC motor with integrated variable frequency drive (fans)",
  "applies_to": "Greenheck Vari-Green single-phase and three-phase EC motors (EC Titanium integrated motor drive) controlled over BACnet MS/TP.",
  "summary": "The Vari-Green (EC Titanium) motor has an integrated drive with an RS-485 port that speaks Modbus RTU or BACnet MS/TP (not both at once). BACnet is enabled with parameter 1103 = 9. The object list is short: run, direction and fault-reset commands, a speed setpoint in % of maximum speed, ramp and speed-limit settings, and readings for speed, frequency, current, power, temperature, energy, run hours, faults and I/O states.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object dictionary from appendix B.6 of the manual (pages 103-104).",
    "The manual prints BI 8 twice: DI3 - Monitor and DI4 - Monitor (status of digital input 4). Only the DI3 row is listed to avoid a duplicate object ID; check where DI4 sits on a live unit.",
    "Several BV names don't match their descriptions: BV 4 'Warning-Monitor' is described as Hand/Auto mode, BV 5 'Ready-Monitor' as the overload warning, and BV 7 and BV 8 are both named 'At-Setpoint-Monitor' (ready status and at-setpoint status). Names, descriptions and state texts are listed as printed.",
    "BO 0 and BO 5 are marked read-only in the table.",
    "AV 0 Output-RPM reads 0 unless the motor rated speed is entered in parameter 9908. AV 8 is printed with unit 'kW/h' and listed here as kWh."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set 1103 Primary Command Source Mode = 9 for BACnet MS/TP, set the address, baud rate and watchdog in 5302 and the device instance in 5840/5899. Command BV 10 run/stop and write the speed setpoint to AV 14 (% of maximum speed); reset faults with BV 14. Read BV 0, AV 1, AV 4, BV 2 and AV 16.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 10",
        "name": "RUN-STOP-Command",
        "why": "Run/stop command (1 = run)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 14",
        "name": "Input-Reference-1",
        "why": "Speed setpoint, % of maximum speed"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 14",
        "name": "Fault-Reset-Command",
        "why": "Fault reset (1 = reset)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 0",
        "name": "Run / Stop-Monitor",
        "why": "Running status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "Output-Freq",
        "why": "Output frequency in Hz"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 4",
        "name": "Output-Current",
        "why": "Motor amps"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 2",
        "name": "OK-Fault-Monitor",
        "why": "Drive fault status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 16",
        "name": "Active-Fault",
        "why": "Active fault code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set 1103 PRIMARY COMMAND SOURCE MODE = 9 (BACnet MS/TP; ramps from 2202/2203). Parameter 9902 then decides whether the speed reference and start/stop come from the network or the terminal strip. BV 4 shows Auto when the drive is under terminal or BACnet control.",
    "heartbeat": "Parameter 5302 includes a watchdog timeout of 0 (disabled), 30, 100, 1000 or 3000 ms. A 't' suffix trips the drive on loss of communication (fault F0010); an 'r' suffix coasts the motor to a stop without a trip.",
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "5302 serial settings: drive address 0-63 (default 1), baud 9.6-115.2 kbps (default 38.4 kbps), watchdog timeout.",
      "BACnet MS/TP format is 8N1; Modbus RTU and BACnet MS/TP cannot run at the same time.",
      "Device instance is set with 5840 (Device Object ID Low) and 5899 (Device Object ID High); the manual's formula reads 5840 x 65536 + 5899.",
      "5841 BACnet maximum masters 0-127; takes effect after a reboot.",
      "Connect RS-485 on the RJ45 port (pins 7 -, 8 +) or terminals T10 (+) / T11 (-); a third 0 V wire to T9 is recommended."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "AV 14 is a percentage of maximum speed, not Hz or rpm.",
      "Min/max speed, ramps and max current (AV 23-33) change motor settings; don't write them cyclically.",
      "BV names are shifted against their descriptions in the manual; check BV 4-8 on a live unit.",
      "The RJ45 port is RS-485, not Ethernet."
    ]
  },
  "source": {
